+### Creating a JSON Patch
+
+`createPatch(from, to)` produces an RFC 6902 JSON Patch that changes `from` into `to`. It validates
+both values as JSON, does not mutate either input, and emits only the necessary operations. Object
+members are compared recursively, while array insertions and removals use indexed operations.
+
+```ts
+import { createPatch } from 'json-toolkit';
+
+createPatch(
+  { profile: { name: 'Ada', title: 'Engineer' } },
+  { profile: { name: 'Ada', team: 'Research' } },
+); // [{ op: 'remove', path: '/profile/title' }, { op: 'add', path: '/profile/team', value: 'Research' }]
+```
+
 ## JSON Merge Patch
 
 `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies an [RFC 7386 JSON Merge Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386)
